    "font size" : 9.963,
    "text color" : "[0.0]",
    "content" : "7. Numerical experiments. We now present a number of numerical experiments to demonstrate the performance of Algorithm 6.1, written in MATLAB language, and compare it with the public C language code of TRJBD in [1]. The experiments will illustrate that Algorithm 6.1 is at least competitive with and can outperform TRJBD considerably in terms of restarts. Since section 4.4 has shown that each restart of IRJBD and TRJBD basically costs the same for the same l and k max , fewer restarts mean higher eﬃciency. The experiments were performed on an AMD Ryzen 7 5800X CPU with 78 GB RAM and 8 cores using the MATLAB R2024a with the machine precision ǫ = 2 . 22 × 10 − 16 under the Ubuntu 20.04.3 LTS 64-bit system."
  }, {
    "type" : "paragraph",
    "pdfua_tag" : "P",
    "id" : 35,
    "page number" : 1,
    "bounding box" : [ 70.333, 248.333, 442.0, 274.333 ],
    "font" : "CMR10",
    "font size" : 9.963,
    "text color" : "[0.0]",
    "content" : "We use some matrices from the SuiteSparse Matrix Collection [6] as A , and L is taken as (cf. [11]):"
  }, {
    "type" : "formula",
    "pdfua_tag" : "Formula",
    "id" : 36,
    "page number" : 1,
    "bounding box" : [ 198.667, 190.333, 296.333, 247.0 ],
    "content" : "3 L 3"
  }, {
    "type" : "paragraph",
    "pdfua_tag" : "P",
    "id" : 37,
    "page number" : 1,
    "bounding box" : [ 69.76, 94.718, 442.0, 182.667 ],
    "font" : "CMR10",
    "font size" : 9.963,
    "text color" : "[0.0]",
    "content" : "which is well conditioned. Table 2 lists the test matrices A and some of their properties, where nnz is the total number of nonzero entries of { A,L } and κ ( A ) = σ max ( A ) σ min ( A ) , available from the SuiteSparse Matrix Collection, is the condition number of A and indicates the level of ill-conditioning of A and reﬂects magnitudes of generalized singular values of { A,L } . In order to ensure that all the A are ﬂat or square, i.e., m   n , we transpose some matrices, denoted by superscript T. Note that the smallest singular value of kneser 8 3 1 T is tiny, which causes that the matrix is numerically row"
  } ]
